# @@name@@

A full-stack app built with [zapline](https://github.com/samsamurai301/zapline):
server-rendered HTML made interactive with [htmx](https://htmx.org), data in
SQL with migrations, and a JSON API with OpenAPI docs. No Node, no build step,
no database server to install: it uses a local SQLite file until you set
`DATABASE_URL`.

```sh
zapline dev          # http://localhost:8080 , rebuilds and restarts on change
cargo test           # every test gets its own in-memory database
```

- <http://localhost:8080/>: the todo app (htmx)
- <http://localhost:8080/docs>: the JSON API, interactive docs
- <http://localhost:8080/health/ready>: readiness, including the database
- Open the todo page in two tabs: changes show up in both at once (`/live/todos`, see `src/routes/todos.rs`)
- <http://localhost:8080/_dev>: the dev console (routes, recent requests, jobs, mail; debug builds only)

Edit a file in `templates/` and refresh: templates reload without a rebuild
in debug builds.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `src/lib.rs` | `app(db)`: builds the `App` (database, templates, static files, docs) |
| `src/main.rs` | Serves `app(..)` with `DATABASE_URL` or `./app.db` |
| `src/routes/` | One module per resource; each exposes `mount(app)` |
| `templates/` | MiniJinja (Jinja2) templates; `{% block %}`s double as htmx fragments |
| `migrations/` | SQL migrations, applied in order at startup |
| `static/` | CSS, images and scripts served under `/static` |
| `tests/` | In-process tests with `app(Database::sqlite_memory()).test()` |

## Common tasks

```sh
zapline g migration add_due_date_to_todos due:string?   # .up.sql + .down.sql
zapline db migrate                   # apply migrations without starting the server
zapline db status                    # what is applied, what is pending
zapline db rollback                  # undo the last migration (its .down.sql)
zapline db reset                     # rebuild the schema and seed it (development)
zapline generate resource project    # CRUD module + tests, registered for you
zapline routes                       # the route table
```

## Postgres

Switch zapline's `sqlite` feature to `postgres` in `Cargo.toml` and set
`DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host/db`. The queries use `$1` placeholders,
which both SQLite and Postgres understand. In the migration, write
`id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY` instead of `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`, and
point the tests at a Postgres with `Database::postgres(url)`.

## Docker

```sh
docker build -t @@name@@ .
docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 -v @@name@@-data:/home/app/data @@name@@
```
